        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0164" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg64"/>

                <head>No. 37.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Young
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 29, 1884.</date>
                        (Received March 31.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 338.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department will learn from the
                    memorials addressed to the throne, which I have the honor to inclose, the extent
                    of the suffering now prevailing in the northern provinces of China, caused by
                    the floods of last year, and the consequent destruction of the crops for
                    hundreds of square miles.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN RUSSELL YOUNG.</signed></closer>



